        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: கட்டளை",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "கட்டளை — kaṭṭaḷai — \"an official order; a command\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "அதிகாரியின் கட்டளையை எல்லோரும் பின்பற்றினார்கள். atikāriyiṉ kaṭṭaḷaiyai ellōrum piṉpaṟṟiṉārkaḷ. Everyone followed the officer's order."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "In computing it also means a command. To give an order is கட்டளை (kaṭṭaḷai) இடு."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "கட்டளை (kaṭṭaḷai) is native Dravidian: DEDR 1147, under கட்டு (kaṭṭu), \"to tie, to bind\", gives கட்டளை (kaṭṭaḷai), \"a code, a rule, regulations\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for saying what happens if."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
